	{
		version = "0.5.49",
		lines = {
			"Charges: \001Orb style\002 has a new look, \001Resource bar\002, now the default unless you chose another style: each charge is a gem in a socket drawn with the game's own class resource art, in a row like combo points, arcane charges, chi or holy power. Lit gems are the charges left, empty sockets the ones used.",
			"Charges: each spell has the art that suits it: Lightning Shield the blue charged combo points, Water Shield the chi orbs in sea green, Earth Shield the druid's combo points in earthy green, Maelstrom Weapon the arcane charges in electric blue white, Inner Fire the druid's combo points in gold, Shadowguard the violet arcane charges and Holy Shield the holy power runes. Where the game lacks a piece of that art, the next set or Flat UI's own glow and ring fill in, so the row always draws.",
			"Charges: the row sits just under the bars of the personal resource display, as wide as they are, and follows them, past a \001Your buffs\002 row on that side, also as Edit Mode moves the display or \001Your buffs\002 changes its place. \001Defensives on you\002, a \001Cooldowns\002 row and the \001Trackers\002 placed at that display sit past it in turn, and close up while \001Only in combat\002 or \001Hide while mounted\002 hides it. New row \001Place\002 (\001Under the personal resource display\002; \001Above the personal resource display\002 or \001Own spot\002, the \001Charges\002 box of /flatui move). While that display is off or hidden, the row goes to its own spot.",
			"Charges: the spell's name shows small above the left end of the row, the charges left as a large number at its right end and the time left small above its right end, outlined in Flat UI's font; where the row is too short for the name and the time side by side, the time sits after the count. New rows \001Name\002 (on) and \001Count\002 (on); \001Time left\002 (on) stays.",
			"Charges: a gained charge or stack lights its gem with a short glow, a used one plays the game's fade of a spent resource with a white flash (with \001Burst as a charge goes\002), the last charge pulses and the row fades out as the buff goes.",
			"Charges: new rows \001Fill the width\002 (on), which spreads the gems from end to end of the bars, each keeping its shape, and \001Gem size\002 (20 px), the gems 3 px apart when not spread.",
			"Charges: new \001Orb style\002 \001Spell art\002: the game's own spell alert art for the buff, Maelstrom Weapon's, fainter on one charge and brighter with each one, with the count, name and time under it. Maelstrom Weapon shows in it while \001Art beside the character\002 or \001Stacks build the art\002 is off; with both on, its stacks build the \001Proc alerts\002 art instead. A buff without such art shows the resource bar.",
			"Charges: Maelstrom Weapon is on a shaman's list. Its stacks show as charges, at least 5 gems, or as many as the game says it can stack, and more once it has had more stacks, at most 10, one more lit with each stack. Its first stack does not pulse, it plays no sound as you spend it, and in a fight it shows its stacks even when it was not on you as the fight began. While the \001Proc alerts\002 art builds up its stacks over the character (\001Art beside the character\002 and \001Stacks build the art\002 on, as they are at first), its stacks show there and not on this page; with either off they show here, as gems, or as its art with \001Spell art\002.",
			"Charges: the orbs of \001Ring round the icon\002, \001Arc over the icon\002 and \001Row under the icon\002 now sit close round the middle and are larger, so ring and orbs read as one, with the spell's name above them while \001Name\002 is on. New row \001Spell icon\002 (off) shows the round icon in the middle; without it the orbs ring the count, which shows at any count while \001Count\002 is on.",
			"Charges: two buffs at once in the resource bar or spell art sit one above the other.",
			"Charges: in a fight, while the game hides your buffs, the game lights the gems of the resource bar and the layers of the spell art, in their own art, and writes the count and time left. Under or above the personal resource display, the row keeps room in a fight for each such buff you have, so one you cast as the fight goes on runs over neither the rows past it nor another buff.",
			"Charges: test mode, a change of its look out of combat and /flatui charges show the sample in the new look; with \001Spell art\002, Maelstrom Weapon gaining a stack each second up to 5, also when test mode is already on as you pick it, or Lightning Shield again while the \001Proc alerts\002 art builds up Maelstrom Weapon's stacks.",
			"A dimmed row can be clicked now: the window goes to the setting it waits for, on its own tab or page, scrolls to it and flashes it, and the strip says what to do, as \"Turn on Fade the block first.\" (for a module's own switch, that it is the switch at the top of its page). A row that another setting replaces, such as \001Custom scale\002 while \001Pixel-perfect scale\002 is on, says why in the strip. Its tip ends \"Click to go to it.\"",
			"\001Search\002 and the \001What's new\002 \001Filter\002 take US spellings and plurals: \"color\", \"gray\", \"center\", \"favor\", \"honor\" and \"armor\" find the colour, grey, centre, favour, honour and armour rows, and \"nameplates\" finds the \001Nameplate\002 rows.",
			"\001Search\002 finds a setting by the names of its choices too, below the rows whose name or tip match, so \"icon rail\" finds \001Sidebar\002. #changed with more words narrows by choice names as well.",
			"\001Search\002 finds the \001Profiles\002 rows by their part of the page: \"switch automatically\" lists \001In a dungeon\002, \001In a raid\002, \001In a battleground or arena\002 and \001Everywhere else\002, the place the switch line in chat names, and \"share\" lists the export and import rows.",
			"While #changed lists settings, the footer shows \001Reset these (9)\002. It asks \"Reset the 9 changed settings listed? Ctrl+Z puts them back.\" (red, and Enter does not answer it), then resets them all as one step. The head counts down, \001Recent changes\002 shows one line, \"Reset of #changed nameplate · 9 settings\", and one Ctrl+Z puts them all back.",
			"Right-click \"Profile: Raid\" on the options window's title bar for the profile list, right under the name. A pick switches at once, or as the fight ends when picked in a fight.",
			"\001Profiles\002: a dim note beside \001Profile in use\002 names who uses the profile, as \"Used by you, Bex and Ivo\" (\"and 2 more\" past three), and its list shows a count after each name, as \"Raid (3)\". \001Delete profile\002 names up to three other characters that use the profile.",
			"Home's \001What's new\002 link names the version it opens, as \"What's new in 0.5.48\", when the installed version has no notes of its own.",
			"These lines about fights now read alike: \"Profiles change after the fight.\", \"In a fight. Finish setup after it.\", \"In a fight. Pick a look after it.\", \001After the fight\002 on the \001Test mode\002 switch and \001Move frames\002, and \"Test mode · paused for the fight\" on the test mode bar, which now has room for it.",
			"The \001Test mode\002 guide lists the Charges, minimap text, ping name, zone text and error text samples, and no longer says zone text and mirror timers have no sample.",
			"Unit frames: a rogue's or a Cat Form druid's combo points now ring Flat UI's target picture, hugging it the way the game's ring hugs its round portrait, in place of a circle up and to the right of it that ran over the target of target. With \001Picture\002 at None they sit at the right end of the health bar. While the character can have combo points, the target of target moves right just far enough to keep the ring clear. Both change out of combat.",
			"Unit frames: with \001Position\002 at \001Beside the target frame\002, the target's and focus's cast bars now keep the spot the game gives them when no target of target shows: just under the frame, or under the aura rows while the unit has auras. Before, they dropped about 51 px whenever the enemy had a target, and jumped as that target came and went. This works in a fight too.",
			"New \001Lost health trail\002 (on/off), under \001Bars\002 on \001All frames: bars and pictures\002, on at first. A pale band shows the chunk of health a hit took on the player, target, focus, pet, target of target, party, party pet and boss frames, and drains smoothly down to the new health over a fraction of a second. Heals still jump up at once, and a new target never drains from the old one's health. It needs \001Flat bars\002, hides with \001Dark health bar, colour shows what is lost\002, and is not on raid cells. Setup draws the band past the Defias Pillager's health.",
			"Unit frames: the raid marker on the target and focus now sits just above Flat UI's picture, as setup draws it, or above the right end of the name row with \001Picture\002 at None. Before, it was over the picture's top edge. The quest mark sits on the picture's lower right corner, and the game's rare star hides while \001Portrait border colour\002, \001Mark after the level\002 or \001Elite or Rare word\002 shows the rank.",
			"Unit frames: /flatui status now has lines for \001Energy tick\002 (in step with the time since the last tick, or waiting for the first tick of 15 energy or more), \001Five-second rule\002, the target of target's \001Position\002, \001Combat and resting icons\002 and the combo points. Where the game sends energy in small steps, so there is no beat to show, the energy tick line and a note now say so, instead of the spark just never showing.",
			"New \001Party power bars for\002 (\001Every member\002; \001Healers only\002) on the \001Party frames\002 tab. \001Healers only\002 keeps the power bar on members with the healer role and fades the others' bars, as \001Hide empty power bar\002 does, also in a fight and as roles change. A member with no role keeps theirs. Setup's \001Party frames\002 step keeps only Bex's.",
			"Unit frames: an enemy someone else has tapped now turns grey in a \001Portrait border\002 of \001Class or reaction colour\002 too (the whole frame's border in \001One frame\002), and on the pet target frame. It turns back if the tap drops.",
			"Unit frames: changing \001Position\002 on the \001Target of target frame\002 tab, or \001Combat and resting icons\002 on the \001Player frame\002 tab, in a fight now says so once while the options window is open: \"Flat UI: the target of target frame moves when the fight ends.\" or \"Flat UI: the combat and resting icons move when the fight ends.\" A new target in a fight stays silent.",
			"Unit frames: in a raid, the game's gold Group tab over the player frame is gone. A small Group 3 in the name font now sits just above the right end of the name row (above the whole frame in \001One frame\002), clear of the level.",
			"Nameplates: on the magnified plate of an enemy you are losing, your \001Target mark\002, its glow and its arrows now hug the magnified bar and stay above every magnified plate. Before, they sat round the small bar under it, with only slivers showing. \001Flash as you change target\002 now plays round the magnified bar, and test mode's sample does the same.",
			"Nameplates: the magnified plate now carries the threat value, outside its bar and raid marker on the side \001Threat value position\002 sets, in the value's colour and font at the magnified size. It also carries the health text inside its bar and the \001Line at Low health below\002. The plate's own name, raid marker and threat value fade out under it over 0.15 seconds and come back as it shrinks away, so no name, marker or number shows twice.",
			"Nameplates: the magnified plate's arrow now stands just over the plate's debuffs, its Overpower icon and an \001Above\002 quest mark, and moves as they come and go, as the plate's own arrow does. Before, it sat on top of them.",
			"Nameplates: while an enemy shown magnified casts, the magnified plate's bottom edge eases up to the health bar's own, so it grows up and sideways and the cast bar stays clear for an interrupt. It grows about the centre again once the cast ends.",
			"Nameplates: the arrow over an enemy you are losing now has a 1 px black edge all round, like the arrows at your target, and its width follows the health bar's height (12 to 24 px), so it reads on snow or lava.",
			"Nameplates: \001Line at Low health below\002 now shows only on enemies in a fight, not on every mob a player rides past or a pack before the pull. It comes as the fight starts and stays one screen pixel wide on your target as the game enlarges it.",
			"Nameplates: new \001Arrows turn red in Low health\002 (on), under \001Arrows at your target\002. Once your target drops under \001Low health below\002, the two arrows turn \001Low health border colour\002, so Execute or Hammer of Wrath range shows on the brightest thing on screen. They turn back as the target heals or you change target. While \001Mark your focus too\002 is on, your focus's arrows turn red the same way.",
			"Nameplates: new \001Arrows move\002 (on), under \001Arrow size\002. On each new target the arrows slide in from 8 px further out over 0.15 seconds, and while the target stays they push in and out by 2 px about once a second. Setup's \001Marks and icons\002 drawing and test mode's sample move the same way.",
			"Nameplates: new \001Mark your focus too\002 (off), under \001Target mark\002. Your focus gets its own outline, glow and arrows in \001Focus colour\002, in a fight too, its arrows turning red in Low health as your target's do. They are left off while your focus is also your target, and /flatui status counts the focuses marked.",
			"Combat text: \001Your interrupts\002 now works at default settings. With \001Where your hits show\002 at \001Over enemies\002, \"Interrupted\" with the icon of your Kick, Counterspell, Pummel or Spell Lock pops over the nameplate of the enemy whose cast you stopped, at the size of the miss words, in \001Interrupt ready colour\002; with \001Scroll area\002 or \001Both\002 it still goes to the Outgoing area. Before, the row stayed greyed out unless the Outgoing area was on. Test mode's target cast bar and /flatui combat test show it once.",
			"New \001Also kicks that stop nothing\002 (on), under \001Your interrupts\002: a kick that went off while your target or focus was casting and left the cast running pops \"Not interrupted\" with its icon in \001Interrupt on cooldown colour\002, and one that came after another player's interrupt pops \"Too late\". It judges only once the game has named who stopped a cast this session, and a cast that cannot be interrupted counts as neither. /flatui status counts both.",
			"New \001Announce your interrupts\002 (\001Off\002; \001Your group's chat\002, \001Party chat only\002, \001Raid chat only\002 or \001Only me\002), under \001Announce to your group\002: sends \"Interrupted Shadow Bolt\" each time the game names you or your pet as the one who stopped an enemy's cast, in any role, at most one line a second, never for another player's kick. /flatui announce reports it, /flatui announce test prints a sample line and /flatui status counts the lines.",
			"New \001Announce your defensives\002 (off), under \001Announce to your group\002: while you count as a tank, using a defensive with a cooldown of a minute or more sends \"Shield Wall up (12 s)\" or \"Last Stand up (20 s)\" to \001Send to\002's chat, at most one line a second.",
			"New \001Only in dungeons and raids\002 (on), under \001Send to\002: the announce lines, the interrupt line too, go out only in a dungeon or raid, so a party out in the world gets none; /flatui announce then says \"nothing sent now, as you are not in a dungeon or raid\".",
			"Cast bars: \001Sound when your focus casts\002 and \001Sound when your target casts\002 no longer play twice in one cast of a caster you have just picked as they step out of range and you close in again. The second sound now plays only when the cast began while your interrupt was down or out of range.",
			"Cast bars: \001Seconds until your interrupt is ready\002 now also counts down on the cast bar of your target's and focus's nameplates, inside its right end beside the cast time, white on a \001Flat nameplate cast bar\002, and goes as the bar turns ready.",
			"Cast bars: a flat fill, on nameplates (\001Flat nameplate cast bar\002, on by default) and on the target and focus bars with \001Flat fill\002, now dips and comes back once over a quarter second as it turns \001Interrupt ready colour\002 when your interrupt comes back or you come into range during the cast. Before, only the strip without \001Flat fill\002 blinked.",
			"Swing timers: with \001Show the timer\002 at \001In combat\002 or \001Only while swinging\002, the timers and their border now fade in over about 0.15 seconds as a fight or the first swing starts, matching the fade out, instead of popping in at full.",
			"Combat text: the tip of \001Spell icons\002 on the \001Scroll areas\002 tab now says it sets the icons in the Outgoing area and on your own heals in the Incoming area, and the row greys out while neither draws icons (\001Where your hits show\002 at \001Over enemies\002 with \001Combat text for you\002 at \001Off\002).",
			"Proc alerts: Maelstrom Weapon is now one of the \001Procs of your class\002. Its art over the character starts as a faint outline and fills a fifth with each stack, with a large outlined count on it in the proc's colour. At 5 stacks the art is full and pulses, the count turns white, the proc sound plays and, with \001Glow on the action button\002, Lightning Bolt, Chain Lightning and the heals glow. Before, it showed only once added under \001Add a proc\002, and it looked the same at 1 stack as at 5. In a fight, while the game hides buffs, the game itself fills the art and writes the number.",
			"New \001Stacks build the art\002 (on), under \001Art beside the character\002 on the \001Proc alerts\002 page. With it off, Maelstrom Weapon's art shows at 5 stacks only, and its stacks show on \001Charges\002.",
			"New \001Seconds left on the art\002 (on): a proc with a time, such as Overpower, Revenge, Riposte or Nature's Grace, counts down its seconds left as a large outlined number on its art, in its colour. The number turns white and grows a little for the last 2 seconds, and fades out with the art. Before, the seconds showed only on the button, and only with the glow on.",
			"Proc alerts: the 4-second preview and test mode step a proc that stacks, such as Maelstrom Weapon, from 1 to 5 stacks.",
			"\001Seconds left on the button\002 now works with \001Glow on the action button\002 off: the button that casts the proc's spell shows the countdown number alone, with no glow and no border. Before, the row was greyed out and showed nothing while the glow was off, as it is by default.",
			"/flatui tracker proc colour, proc time and the new proc sound and proc reset now work on the procs of your class too. Name the proc, even a name with spaces, or give the number \001Remove a proc\002 shows, as /flatui tracker proc colour Execute ff3030 or proc sound Clearcasting none. Before, they found only procs you added, and no proc could get its own sound. The art, the border and the button glow take a new colour at once.",
			"Bar block: holding the key set in \001While a key is held\002 on the \001Fading\002 page now also brings a fading block, its panel and the experience bar under it back to full. Before, every faded frame came back except the bars of the block.",
			"Bar block: a block now closes up round a bar that \001Hide empty bars\002 hides. It stacks only the bars that show, and its panel, the experience bar and the stance and pet bars sit tight round them. The empty space no longer brings a faded block back under the mouse. When a spell or item is picked up, the empty bars come back in their places.",
			"\001Hide empty bars\002: the first time bars hide for being empty, chat says so once for the character, names them and says how to keep them. /flatui status gains the line \"Hidden for being empty: action bars 3 and 4.\"",
			"Faint empty buttons now rise to full over about 0.12 seconds when a spell or item is picked up, and settle back over 0.2 seconds when it is dropped. Before, they snapped across every bar in one frame.",
			"\001Bars come back together\002: the bar under the mouse and the rest now start and end their fade on the same tick. Before, the bar under the mouse came up one step ahead of the others.",
			"Trackers: the \001Healthstone\002 tracker now counts Improved Healthstone stones, yours or another warlock's, so it no longer shows red, says 'Healthstone is missing' at ready checks or tries to make a second stone while one is in your bags. Trackers you added earlier pick up the new stones by themselves.",
			"Trackers: with \001Shape\002 at Bar, a tracker's bar now glides as it fills and empties instead of jumping, with a thin bright spark riding its edge as on the game's cast bar. A bar filled by \001Charges\002 shows a thin notch between charges (2 to 10), so 2 of 3 Lightning Shield, Inner Fire or Shadowguard charges reads at a glance.",
			"Trackers: \001Sound\002 now says that only Raid warning, Alarm and Whisper warning play for a buff in a fight. Picking Spell alert, Chimes, Bell or Warhorn, on the page or for one tracker, with a buff sound on now prints one chat line saying it plays between fights only, and /flatui tracker check names the trackers left silent in a fight.",
			"Your buffs: \001Sound when one ends\002 now leaves a buff out only when its tracker really plays a sound as it drops. A tracker with \001Sound when it drops\002 off, or with a sound the game does not play in a fight, no longer silences it, so a rogue hears Slice and Dice fall off.",
			"Absorb shields: new \001Shield stripes\002 (on). Each bar's fill and the total now carry the game's striped shield pattern, as its later frames draw absorbs, tinted by school, with a soft bright edge where the fill ends. The bars the game draws in a fight have it too.",
			"Cooldown pulse: new \001When it pulses\002 (\001Always\002; \001In combat only\002 or \001Not while mounted or in a city\002), so the Hearthstone and buffs cast between pulls no longer have to flash mid-screen. Test pulses and the samples of the look still show, and /flatui pulse list names the rule.",
			"Cooldown pulse: new \001Burst as it shows\002 (on). The game's star flash, the one its own cooldowns show as they end, now bursts once over the icon as a pulse comes in, in the item's quality colour for an item.",
			"Defensives on you: new \001Time left\002 (\001On the icon\002; \001Thin bar under the icon\002 or \001Off\002). The time left was always a large number over the icon. It can now be a thin bar in the \001Bar texture\002 of \001Your buffs\002, so the two rows match, with the caster's name moved under it. The samples follow the choice.",
			"Windows: with \001Item level on equipped gear\002 on, the Character window now shows your own average item level under your level ('Item level 58.3'), in \001Item level colour\002, to set beside the one the Inspect window shows. It updates as you change gear.",
			"Fix: the threat list's warning sounds (\001Warning sound\002 as you lose an enemy or near aggro, and \001Sound when you lose an enemy\002) no longer go quiet when another Flat UI sound played just before, such as \001Entering combat sound\002 at the pull or a party cooldown ending. They play at most one every third of a second among themselves.",
			"Party cooldowns: \001Share cooldowns with the party\002 now also works in a raid. Members of your subgroup who run Flat UI share their cooldowns with the time left, and the icon tooltip says \"Shared by Flat UI\", as in a party. /flatui party list says who shares.",
			"Threat list: the tooltip of a small enemy row, or of a row of \001Enemies you fight\002, now follows its row as the enemies re-sort, so it no longer names the wrong enemy or an old state.",
			"Threat list: as your taunt lands, your bar flashes once in a light shade of \001Threat you want\002, with no sound. So does an enemy row you take back from Lost: in \001Enemies you fight\002 as it turns Slipping or Held, and under your target while it is still Slipping, as it is right after a taunt. Test mode shows your bar's flash on the step after the sample Mage's turn.",
			"Threat list: when a tank's list falls back to the enemy they are losing most, the title now names who holds it in red, as \"Defias Pillager > Mage\", and that member's bar keeps a steady red wash, so the tank sees whom to taunt off without targeting it. \001Calm when another tank takes it\002 still keeps another tank calm.",
			"Healer mana: pointing at a bar now names the healer in their class colour with their mana (\"Mana hidden in a fight\" where the game hides it), Dead or Offline, the seconds left on a drink, and whether they are under \001Low mana at\002 or \001Ready at\002. Pointing at the \"+3 more\" line lists those healers with their mana. Clicks still go through to the world.",
			"Healer mana: Shift-clicking the title puts every healer's mana in the chat line, ready to send, as \"Healer mana: Eli 82%, Mara 47% (drinking 12s), Fay Dead\". In a fight, where the game hides the numbers, it says so instead.",
			"Threat list: in a raid, a tank's enemy rows are read twice a second instead of five times, and the member list is kept until the roster or a pet changes, so big pulls no longer hitch.",
			"New /flatui party reset and /flatui enemy reset put the abilities of \001Party cooldowns\002 and \001Enemy cooldowns\002 back as Flat UI ships them, undoing every add, hide and typed cooldown, and say what they undid.",
			"Threat list: at the end of a fight, the small enemy rows now fade out with the rest of the window instead of vanishing first and making the box snap shorter.",
			"Bags: Escape now closes an open menu of the bag or bank window first, such as a section title's menu, the Characters picker, a colour list or a bag's settings, and the bags stay open. A second Escape closes them. In a fight the first Escape still closes both.",
			"Bags: a section title's right-click menu now has \001Order: By kind\002. It opens the four choices of \001Order in a section\002, ticked, and a pick re-sorts both windows at once as one change in Recent changes, so Ctrl+Z undoes it.",
			"Bags: the long menu of a section title now has faint thin lines between its groups: moving the section, this section's own lines, the lines for every section, the lists, and your own sections' lines.",
			"Bags: when your bags fill and you carry junk, the chat line now goes on to say how much room it takes and what it is worth: \"Flat UI: your bags are full (0 of 80 free). Junk takes 6 slots, worth 1g 4s: Sell junk at a merchant frees them.\"",
			"Bags: \001Your sell list\002 and \001Never sold\002 in the Junk title's menu now show each item with its icon and its name in its quality's colour, and pointing at one shows the item's tooltip. A click takes it off as before, and the list opens again without it until it is empty, so taking off five items no longer needs five right-clicks.",
			"Bags: the Free label in the footer now lights under the mouse like your gold. In Sections, a click switches \001Free slots\002 between One per kind of bag and Every free slot, as one change in Recent changes, and its tooltip says so.",
			"Bags: a running Deposit or Take out now counts down on its button, as \"Stop (12)\", the way Sell junk does.",
			"Bags: putting back a single item in \001Items placed by hand\002 can now be brought back. The first line offers it (Bring back the placement you took off Potions), the emptied section keeps its title, and the chat line says so.",
			"Bags: a kept search with a bar, such as (cloth || leather) #gear, now shows one bar on the Bags page's \001Custom sections\002 line and in its chat line, not two.",
			"Bags: double-clicking the width grip to put the width back is always one change in Recent changes, so one Ctrl+Z undoes it.",
			"New \001Bar art\002 row on the \001Experience and menu bars\002 page (\001Flat fill\002 by default). \001The game's modern art\002 draws Flat UI's experience and reputation bars with the game's own modern fills on its dark bar background, in place of \001Bar texture\002, \001Experience colour\002 and the standing colours. Experience is the purple fill, and the blue rested fill while you are rested. Reputation takes the red, orange, yellow, green or blue fill of its standing. The tooltip, the quest stretch, the gains, the level flash and the text work on top as before, and test mode's sample bar uses the art too. \001Bar background\002 off leaves out the dark background. Where the game has no such art, the bar keeps its flat fill and /flatui status says so.",
			"Text around the map: each place row (\001Coordinates place\002, \001Durability place\002, \001Frame rate place\002, \001Time place\002) now also offers \001On the map, at the bottom\002. The line sits just inside the map's bottom edge, outlined so it reads over the ground, with its tooltip, click and light under the mouse as before. On a round map it is raised to stay inside the circle. Lines there stack upward and take no room under the map, so the addon button row and the zone name keep their place.",
			"Text around the map: a line that comes into view, such as the coordinates as you leave a dungeon, durability at 50% or a test mode sample, now fades in over 0.15 seconds instead of popping on. Hiding stays instant, so the lines below close up at once.",
			"Minimap: where the game refuses the square mask and the map keeps its round one, the name of who pinged now stays inside the round edge. Before, it was kept inside a square there and could sit outside the circle.",
			"\001Quest count\002: with \001Quests ready in the count\002 on, pointing at the count now lists up to five of the quests ready to hand in by name, in \001Quest colour\002 (\"Kobold Camp Cleanup\"), then \"and 2 more\", above the click hint. The list stays up to date while they point at it.",
			"/flatui hide tracker (or minimap, buffs, objective tracker, or any row's name or part of it) now hides that frame or shows it again, from chat or a macro, and says which: \"Flat UI: Objective tracker is hidden. /flatui hide tracker shows it again.\" or \"Flat UI: Objective tracker shows again.\". In a fight the change waits for its end. /flatui hide list names the frames that are hidden. A plain /flatui hide still opens the \001Hidden frames\002 page.",
			"\001/flatui move\002: with several boxes selected, a new \001Hide these\002 button beside \001Reset these\002 hides every selected frame that has a row on the \001Hidden frames\002 page. It reads \001Show these\002 once all of them are hidden, and is dimmed when none of them has a row. Chat names once any selected frame without a row: \"Flat UI: Chat has no row on the Hidden frames page, so it stays.\"",
			"\001/flatui move\002: Ctrl-A now selects every box that can move, including boxes behind the toolbar or the inspector. That is every shown box except those of frames the game places and those hidden with their eye in the frame list. The inspector reads \"24 frames selected\", and the arrow keys, the align buttons and \001Reset these\002 work on them all. Escape lets go as before. The \001Frame list\002 tooltip mentions it.",
			"With \001Error text size\002 or \001Zone title size\002 away from 100%, a new font picked on the \001Fonts\002 page now reaches the red error text, the yellow quest lines and the zone titles at once, at their size. Before, they kept the old face until a /reload.",
			"The hit table no longer catches the mouse once it fades out in a fight (the target dies, they drop it, or \001Show\002 hides it): enemies and the world behind that spot get their mouseover and tooltip again at once. A table that first shows during a fight now shows its own tooltip with \001Tooltip when you point at it\002.",
			"New \001Raid marker on the name\002 (on): a unit's tooltip shows the skull, moon or other raid marker it carries as a small icon before its name, under \001Unit colours\002 on the \001Tooltips\002 page.",
			"New \001Away and busy after the name\002 (on): a player who is away or busy has a dim <AFK> or <DND> after their name on their tooltip, as \"Mara <AFK>\".",
			"New \001Flash the game's icon when you are named\002 (on), under \001Mentions\002 on the \001Chat text\002 page: while the game is in the background, its icon on the taskbar or dock flashes for a line that names them, as it does for a whisper, at most once every 10 seconds.",
			"\001Show recent chat after a reload\002: each name in the restored lines is now a player link, in its class colour where the game knows it, so a click whispers and a right-click opens the player menu as on a live line. \001Copy recent chat\002 still copies plain [Name].",
			"\001Duration format\002 \001Minutes and seconds (28:41)\002: a buff of an hour or more now reads as hours and minutes, as 1h42 or 1h05, down to 59:59, in place of 2h, then 90m to 60m. Test mode's samples match.",
			"The \001Copy recent chat\002 box and the web address box now fade in with the game's window sounds, play the closing sound as they shut, and have a small cross at the top right that lights under the mouse and closes the box.",
			"\001Carrot on a Stick while riding\002: the trinket it replaced is now kept for each character, so it goes back on as they get off after a /reload or a disconnect during the ride too.",
			"\001Queue line on trinket tooltips\002 no longer shows on the rows of the \001Trinket queue\002 window, which show the same already. It still shows on trinkets in the bags and on the Character window.",
			"Consumables bar: a button now lights up under the mouse with an accent border and a soft white wash. While its key or the mouse button is held it darkens and sinks a pixel, so every use of the bar is felt.",
			"Consumables bar: an oil, sharpening stone, weightstone or poison now goes straight onto your weapon. A click puts it on your main hand and a right-click on a weapon in your off hand, with no glowing hand to aim, as the tooltip says (\"Click: on your main hand. Right-click: on your off hand.\"). Shift+right-click still puts it on your list or takes it off.",
			"Consumables bar: an elixir, flask or scroll whose buff is on you now has a green border and the minutes left at its top right, as \"14m\". It goes plain again as the buff runs out, so a missing buff stands out.",
			"Consumables bar: the tooltip of an item that is cooling down now says \"Ready in 1:42\" in warm text and counts down while the mouse stays. It says \"Ready\" in green as the cooldown ends.",
			"Consumables bar: \001Show count\002 now shows a count of 3 or fewer in amber, so the last few flasks stand out before the red 0. The count goes white again after a restock.",
			"Data panels: the invisible click area of the \001Hearthstone\002 slot now goes with its panel. Before, turning the panel or the page off in a fight, or the page stopping on an error in one, left a click area there after the fight that could use the Hearthstone.",
			"World and cursor: with nothing glowing near you, ticking \001Glow on the nearest object\002 or changing \001Glow colour\002 or \001Glow size\002 out of a fight with the options window open now shows the glow for 3 seconds a little above the middle of the screen, at its new size. With \001By what it is\002 it steps through green, copper, gold and white.",
			"World and cursor: \001Maximum camera distance\002 ticked in a fight now says \"Flat UI: Maximum camera distance changes when the fight ends.\" When the fight ends the camera glides out, as it does when ticked at any other time.",
			"World and cursor: the \001Lava tick timer\002 box in /flatui move is now as wide and tall as \001Lava bar width\002 and \001Lava bar height\002 make the bar, so it lines up with other frames and the snap guides.",
			"World and cursor: \001Cursor ring colour\002 now greys out with \"Needs Class colour off.\" while \001Class colour\002 is on, and sits under it.",
			"The queue eye by the minimap is now followed the same safe way as every other game frame Flat UI keeps in place: with the game's taint log on, Flat UI leaves its methods alone and counts them in /flatui status, while the regular check still keeps the eye where you put it.",
