			"Hit table: in a fight it now shows the numbers the game gave out of one, in the stance or form you are in where it has them, in place of ? in every column, as the enemy tooltips already did. It reads them while it is hidden too, so with \001Show\002 at \001In combat\002 it has numbers from the first fight.",
			"Hit table: a number the game has not given out of a fight since you logged in or reloaded, as after a reload in a fight, shows a light dash in place of ?. A dark dash still marks a part the attack cannot have, as a parry from behind.",
			"Hit table: a druid out of Bear and Cat Form now gets a line for their swings as well as their spells while they hold a weapon. This works under the player frame, on enemy tooltips and in the hit lines of \001Explain the stats\002. Under the player frame and on enemy tooltips there is no line for special attacks out of those forms.",
			"Hit table: the title says whose level it is, as \"Target level 6\" (before, \"Level 6\").",
			"Hit table: new \001Tooltip when you point at it\002 (on), under \001When it shows\002. Pointing at the table says what Cap and the dashes mean, and why a number is from before the fight or not given, as /flatui status does. While the table shows, an enemy right behind it gets this tooltip in place of its own. Clicks still go through to the world.",
			"Hit table: the tip of \001Background and border\002 explains the thin red line that can show under a number in a fight. It is the bar of an enemy's nameplate far behind the table, seen through its see-through background. \001Own border and background\002 on the \001Minimap\002 page, with a higher \001Background opacity\002, makes the background more solid.",
			"The game's big hit numbers no longer flash over your portrait and your pet's: \001Hit numbers on player and pet portraits\002 (on the \001All frames: icons and auras\002 tab of \001Unit frames\002) is now off at first. Turn it on to have them back.",
			"In a fight, the game's crossed swords now sit just above the top right corner of the player portrait, no longer on the picture, and its sleeping letters do the same while resting. In \001One frame\002 they sit above the whole frame. The new \001Combat and resting icons\002 row on the \001Player frame\002 tab can put them back where the game draws them. A change made in a fight applies as it ends.",
			"The target of target frame now sits just right of the target frame with their tops in line, no longer floating below and to the right, and the focus target sits beside the focus frame, in either \001Frame style\002. It goes with the target frame wherever \001/flatui move\002 puts it. The new \001Position\002 row on the \001Target of target frame\002 tab can leave it on the game's spot. It moves out of combat.",
			"Action bars: empty buttons are faint by default, as \001Empty buttons\002 (\001Faint\002) and \001Faint empty button opacity\002 (50%) say. Before, Edit Mode's \001Always show buttons\002, on at first, kept them at full, so a half-filled bar looked like a wall of empty boxes.",
			"Action bars: with Edit Mode's \001Always show buttons\002 off (in Edit Mode, or with \001Show empty buttons\002 on the \001Bar block\002 page), empty buttons on Flat UI's bars now hide, as the game's do, instead of showing faint.",
			"Action bars: an empty button no longer shows its key, so the bars are no longer covered in labels such as s-1, s-WU and WD. New \001Hotkeys on empty buttons\002 (off), under \001Hotkeys\002 on the \001Button text\002 page, shows them again.",
			"Action bars: while a spell or item is on the cursor, every empty button is at full and shows its key, so you can see where it goes and which key it has.",
			"Action bars: new \001Hide empty bars\002 (on), under \001Buttons\002 on the \001Action bars\002 page, for Flat UI's buttons. Bars 2 to 8 hide while none of their buttons holds anything, and show again as soon as a spell or item is on the cursor, so you can fill them. They also show in /flatui move and in Edit Mode. The main bar always shows.",
